Phantrix's Apple backend integrates the official WireGuard
implementation for Apple platforms, WireGuard for iOS and macOS
(wireguard-apple), which is MIT licensed.

The following files are vendored from that project, under its MIT
license, with only the platform-specific labels adapted to
Phantrix:

  Sources/Shared/Keychain.swift
  Sources/Shared/FileManager+Extension.swift
  Sources/Shared/ErrorNotifier.swift
  Sources/Shared/NotificationToken.swift
  Sources/Shared/Logger.swift
  Sources/Shared/String+ArrayConversion.swift
  Sources/Shared/NETunnelProviderProtocol+Extension.swift
  Sources/Shared/TunnelConfiguration+WgQuickConfig.swift
  Sources/Extension/PhantrixPacketTunnelProvider.swift
  (adapted from Sources/WireGuardNetworkExtension/PacketTunnelProvider.swift)

The WireGuardKit Swift package, which provides the
TunnelConfiguration, InterfaceConfiguration, PeerConfiguration,
PrivateKey, PublicKey, IPAddressRange, DNSServer, Endpoint and
WireGuardAdapter types these files build on, is added as a
package dependency, not vendored here. It is built from
https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-apple with the
WireGuardGoBridge<PLATFORM> external build target described in
the project README, because Swift Package Manager cannot build
the wireguard-go-bridge library itself.

